TAGLINE

A style pack of the motion-explainer library: portable rules plus tokens, no build attached. `style.json` carries the canvas, palette and fonts so any tool reads one source; `docs/style-guide.md` carries the rules. It scripts, storyboards and prompts from day one.

## The DNA

The six rules that make any topic read as this style. Everything else in `docs/style-guide.md` is a default you may change.

1. LOOK_RULE_1
2. LOOK_RULE_2
3. LOOK_RULE_3
4. LOOK_RULE_4
5. MOTION_RULE
6. TYPE_RULE

## Measured from the reference (`style_ref.py`)

Canvas CANVAS · shots median MEDIAN_SHOT · CUT_RATE · motion MOTION · saturation SATURATION

The reference's rhythm and tonality, not a target to hit exactly: what a later episode compares against to tell drift from choice.

## Tokens

In `style.json` → `extra.tokens`, one role each. Read them from there, never from this file.

| token | hex | role |
|---|---|---|
| `bg` | `FULL_BG` | TODO |
| `ink` | `FULL_INK` | TODO |
| `cream` | `FULL_CREAM` | TODO |
| `hero` | `FULL_HERO` | TODO |
| `cap` | `FULL_CAP` | TODO |
| `tag` | `FULL_TAG` | TODO |

Fonts: `extra.fonts` (`display`, `text`) by family description; ship a file only when you have the licence.

## The gate

```sh
$MOTION_PY $MOTION_LIB/tools/style_ref.py lint ../STYLE_NAME
$MOTION_PY $MOTION_LIB/tools/style_ref.py probe ../STYLE_NAME path/to/one-still.png
```

`lint` must pass before an episode leans on this pack. `probe` runs once any renderer produces a still: a token it cannot find in the frame means that renderer ignored the palette.

## Files

| file | what it gives |
|---|---|
| `docs/style-guide.md` | the authority: look, colour, type, motion, beat, signature move, traps |
| `docs/style-prompt.md` | the same DNA as copy-paste blocks for another agent or generator |
| `style.json` | manifest: canvas, tokens, fonts, status, reference numbers |

